@page "/accounting"

@*
    At /accounting and not /accounts, because /accounts is the user-account list and has been
    since section 4. Two pages on one route is a routing exception at startup, and the first
    version of this page collided exactly there.
*@
@using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations
@using JiranisokoTech.Application.Abstractions
@using JiranisokoTech.Application.Accounting
@using JiranisokoTech.Application.Authorization
@using JiranisokoTech.Domain.Money
@using JiranisokoTech.Infrastructure.Accounting
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = PermissionClaim.PolicyPrefix + Permissions.AccountingView)]
@inject AccountingQueries Queries
@inject AccountingService Service
@inject IClock Clock
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@*
    The chart of accounts, and what the firm earned and spent.

    Section 18 had invoices, payments and expense claims and no way to say what any of it was
    for: "we spent four million shillings last quarter" was answerable and "on what" was not.

    There is no general ledger and no balance anywhere, which is the decision of this section
    rather than an omission. A stored balance is a number that can disagree with the documents
    it was added up from, and on the day it does nobody can tell which is wrong — so every
    figure below is summed from the invoices, claims and charges themselves.
*@

<PageTitle>Accounts — Jiranisoko Delivery</PageTitle>

<div class="page-head">
    <h1>Accounts</h1>
    <p class="subtle">@Summary</p>
</div>

@if (Refusal is not null)
{
    <p class="refusal" role="alert">@Refusal</p>
}

<section class="standing">
    <h2>Income and expenditure</h2>

    @*
        Named on its face rather than left to be assumed. Income is what was invoiced and
        expenditure is what was claimed or fell due, so this is an accrual view on both sides —
        mixing invoiced income against paid costs gives a margin that is neither, and is wrong
        in the direction that always flatters.
    *@
    <p class="subtle">
        Invoiced income and accrued costs, @Report.From.ToString("d MMM yyyy") to
        @Report.To.ToString("d MMM yyyy"), in @Report.Currency. Drafts are not counted.
    </p>

    <form method="get" class="filters">
        <label>
            <span>From</span>
            <input type="date" name="from" value="@Report.From.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")" />
        </label>
        <label>
            <span>To</span>
            <input type="date" name="to" value="@Report.To.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")" />
        </label>
        <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">Show</button>
    </form>

    @if (Report.IsEmpty)
    {
        <p class="empty">
            Nothing was invoiced or claimed in that window.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <table class="grid">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Income and expenditure</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Code</th>
                    <th scope="col">Account</th>
                    <th scope="col">In</th>
                    <th scope="col">Out</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var line in Report.Income)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>@line.Code</code></td>
                        <td>@line.Name</td>
                        <td class="number">@line.Total</td>
                        <td class="number">—</td>
                    </tr>
                }
                @foreach (var line in Report.Expenditure)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>@line.Code</code></td>
                        <td>@line.Name</td>
                        <td class="number">—</td>
                        <td class="number">@line.Total</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
            <tfoot>
                <tr>
                    <td></td>
                    <td><strong>Total</strong></td>
                    <td class="number"><strong>@Report.TotalIncome</strong></td>
                    <td class="number"><strong>@Report.TotalExpenditure</strong></td>
                </tr>
            </tfoot>
        </table>

        @if (Report.Payroll.MinorUnits > 0)
        {
            @*
                Its own line rather than a row in the table above, because payroll is not an
                account — an account is something somebody codes an invoice or a claim against —
                and because the firm's largest cost should not be one row among forty.

                One figure for the firm and no breakdown behind it. A payroll line split by
                department would undo the reasoning the project costing is built on: a
                department of two is one subtraction from an individual's salary, and this page
                is read by people who do not hold employees.pay.
            *@
            <p class="subtle">
                Of which payroll: @Report.Payroll
                <span class="subtle">gross plus the firm's own contributions</span>
            </p>
        }

        @*
            Called the difference and never profit. Payroll is in it now — section 22, which
            used to be the largest of the three reasons this word was chosen — but there is
            still no depreciation and no corporation tax, and being wrong by less is not the
            same as being right.
        *@
        <p class="subtle">Difference: @Report.Difference. This is not a profit figure.</p>

        @if (Report.LeftOutForCurrency > 0)
        {
            <p class="subtle">
                @Report.LeftOutForCurrency document(s) in another currency were left out.
                Adding currencies together would be a figure with no meaning.
            </p>
        }
    }
</section>

<section class="standing">
    <h2>The chart</h2>

    <AuthorizeView Policy="@ManagePolicy" Context="mayOpen">
        <EditForm Model="Opening" method="post" OnValidSubmit="Open" FormName="open"
                  class="inline">
            <InputText @bind-Value="Opening.Code" placeholder="4200" />
            <InputText @bind-Value="Opening.Name" placeholder="Software subscriptions" />
            <InputSelect @bind-Value="Opening.Kind">
                <option value="@AccountKind.Expense">Expense</option>
                <option value="@AccountKind.Income">Income</option>
            </InputSelect>
            <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">Open it</button>
        </EditForm>
    </AuthorizeView>

    @if (Chart.Count == 0)
    {
        <p class="empty">
            No accounts yet. Until there are, everything invoiced and claimed appears on the
            report above as not coded to an account.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <table class="grid">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">The chart of accounts</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Code</th>
                    <th scope="col">Account</th>
                    <th scope="col">Side</th>
                    <th scope="col">Coded to it</th>
                    <th scope="col"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var account in Chart)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>@account.Code</code></td>
                        <td>
                            @account.Name
                            @if (!account.IsOpen)
                            {
                                <span class="pill pill--quiet">retired</span>
                            }
                        </td>
                        <td>@account.Kind</td>
                        <td class="number">@account.CodedToIt</td>
                        <td>
                            <AuthorizeView Policy="@ManagePolicy" Context="mayChange">
                                @if (account.IsOpen)
                                {
                                    @*
                                        Retired, never deleted. An account with history behind
                                        it cannot be removed without making last year's report
                                        unreadable, and "retire" is what people mean when they
                                        ask to delete one.
                                    *@
                                    <EditForm Model="Nothing" method="post"
                                              FormName="@($"retire-{account.Id}")"
                                              OnValidSubmit="() => Retire(account.Id)"
                                              class="inline">
                                        <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">
                                            Retire
                                        </button>
                                    </EditForm>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <EditForm Model="Nothing" method="post"
                                              FormName="@($"reopen-{account.Id}")"
                                              OnValidSubmit="() => Reopen(account.Id)"
                                              class="inline">
                                        <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">
                                            Reopen
                                        </button>
                                    </EditForm>
                                }

                                <EditForm Model="Nothing" method="post"
                                          FormName="@($"rename-{account.Id}")"
                                          OnValidSubmit="() => Rename(account.Id)" class="inline">
                                    <input type="text" name="name" placeholder="New name" />
                                    <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">
                                        Rename
                                    </button>
                                </EditForm>
                            </AuthorizeView>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    }
</section>

<section class="standing">
    <h2>Standing costs</h2>

    @*
        Rent, a domain renewal, a subscription: money that leaves every month whether or not
        anybody remembers it. These used to be expense claims typed from memory, which means the
        month somebody was on leave is a month the cost report is wrong — and a cost missing from
        a report looks exactly like a cost that was not incurred.

        Nothing here pays anything. A charge is a record that the cost fell due on a date, and
        settling one is somebody saying the money went out; this system does not touch a bank
        and would be claiming something it cannot know if it said otherwise.
    *@
    <AuthorizeView Policy="@ManagePolicy" Context="maySchedule">
        @if (Expenses.Any(one => one.Kind == AccountKind.Expense && one.IsOpen))
        {
            <EditForm Model="Scheduling" method="post" OnValidSubmit="Schedule"
                      FormName="schedule" class="panel stack">
                <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                <div class="fields">
                    <label>
                        <span>Account</span>
                        <InputSelect @bind-Value="Scheduling.AccountId">
                            @foreach (var one in Expenses.Where(
                                one => one.Kind == AccountKind.Expense && one.IsOpen))
                            {
                                <option value="@one.Id">@one.Code — @one.Name</option>
                            }
                        </InputSelect>
                    </label>

                    <label>
                        <span>How often</span>
                        <InputSelect @bind-Value="Scheduling.Every">
                            <option value="@Recurrence.Monthly">Monthly</option>
                            <option value="@Recurrence.Quarterly">Quarterly</option>
                            <option value="@Recurrence.Annually">Annually</option>
                        </InputSelect>
                    </label>

                    <label>
                        <span>Starts</span>
                        <InputDate @bind-Value="Scheduling.StartsOn" />
                    </label>
                </div>

                <div class="fields">
                    <label>
                        <span>What it is</span>
                        <InputText @bind-Value="Scheduling.Description" placeholder="Office rent" />
                        <ValidationMessage For="() => Scheduling.Description" />
                    </label>

                    <label>
                        <span>Paid to</span>
                        <InputText @bind-Value="Scheduling.Payee" placeholder="Landlord" />
                        <ValidationMessage For="() => Scheduling.Payee" />
                    </label>

                    <label>
                        <span>How much (KES)</span>
                        <InputNumber @bind-Value="Scheduling.Amount" />
                        <ValidationMessage For="() => Scheduling.Amount" />
                    </label>
                </div>

                <button type="submit">Put it on the timetable</button>
            </EditForm>
        }
    </AuthorizeView>

    @if (Standing.Count == 0)
    {
        <p class="empty">
            No standing costs. Rent, domains and subscriptions put here are raised by the
            scheduler on the day they fall due, and caught up if it has been off.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <table class="grid">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Standing costs</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">What</th>
                    <th scope="col">Paid to</th>
                    <th scope="col">How much</th>
                    <th scope="col">How often</th>
                    <th scope="col">Next due</th>
                    <th scope="col"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var cost in Standing)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            @cost.Description
                            @if (!cost.IsActive)
                            {
                                <span class="pill pill--quiet">paused</span>
                            }
                        </td>
                        <td class="subtle">@cost.Payee</td>
                        <td class="number">@cost.Amount</td>
                        <td>@cost.Every</td>
                        <td>
                            @(cost.NextDueOn?.ToString("d MMM yyyy") ?? "—")
                            @if (cost.Unsettled > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="pill pill--wait">@cost.Unsettled unsettled</span>
                            }
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            <AuthorizeView Policy="@ManagePolicy" Context="mayAmend">
                                @if (cost.IsActive)
                                {
                                    <EditForm Model="Nothing" method="post"
                                              FormName="@($"pause-{cost.Id}")"
                                              OnValidSubmit="() => Pause(cost.Id)" class="inline">
                                        <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">
                                            Pause
                                        </button>
                                    </EditForm>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <EditForm Model="Nothing" method="post"
                                              FormName="@($"resume-{cost.Id}")"
                                              OnValidSubmit="() => Resume(cost.Id)" class="inline">
                                        <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">
                                            Resume
                                        </button>
                                    </EditForm>
                                }

                                @if (cost.OldestUnsettled is { } charge)
                                {
                                    @*
                                        Settling the oldest rather than offering a list. Standing
                                        costs are settled in the order they fell due, and a
                                        picker would invite somebody to mark March paid while
                                        February is still open.
                                    *@
                                    <EditForm Model="Nothing" method="post"
                                              FormName="@($"settle-{cost.Id}")"
                                              OnValidSubmit="() => Settle(cost.Id, charge)"
                                              class="inline">
                                        <button type="submit" class="button button--quiet">
                                            Mark @cost.OldestUnsettledOn?.ToString("MMM") paid
                                        </button>
                                    </EditForm>
                                }
                            </AuthorizeView>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    }
</section>

@code {
    private const string ManagePolicy =
        PermissionClaim.PolicyPrefix + Permissions.AccountingManage;

    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? Request { get; set; }

    [SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    private DateOnly? From { get; set; }

    [SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    private DateOnly? To { get; set; }

    private OpenInput _opening = new();

    [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "open")]
    private OpenInput Opening
    {
        get => _opening;
        set => _opening = value ?? new OpenInput();
    }

    private object Nothing { get; } = new();

    private List<AccountRow> Chart { get; set; } = [];

    private List<StandingCostRow> Standing { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The expense accounts a standing cost may be coded to.</summary>
    private List<AccountRow> Expenses => Chart;

    private ScheduleInput _scheduling = new();

    [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "schedule")]
    private ScheduleInput Scheduling
    {
        get => _scheduling;
        set => _scheduling = value ?? new ScheduleInput();
    }

    private IncomeAndExpenditure Report { get; set; } =
        new(default, default, "KES", [], [], 0);

    private string? Refusal { get; set; }

    private string Summary => Chart.Count == 0
        ? "What money is classified as, and what the firm earned and spent."
        : $"{Chart.Count(one => one.IsOpen)} open, "
            + $"{Chart.Count(one => !one.IsOpen)} retired.";

    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync() => await LoadAsync();

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        /*
         * This quarter by default rather than this month. A month is too short to read a
         * pattern from and long enough that a bad one has already happened; a quarter is what
         * anybody asking this question is actually asking about.
         */
        var today = Clock.Today;

        var from = From ?? new DateOnly(today.Year, ((today.Month - 1) / 3 * 3) + 1, 1);
        var to = To ?? today;

        Chart = await Queries.AccountsAsync();
        Standing = await Queries.StandingCostsAsync();
        Report = await Queries.ReportAsync(from, to, "KES");

        Scheduling.AccountId ??= Chart
            .FirstOrDefault(one => one.Kind == AccountKind.Expense && one.IsOpen)?.Id;

        Scheduling.StartsOn ??= today;
    }

    private Task Open() => TryAsync(() => Service.OpenAccountAsync(
        Opening.Code, Opening.Name, Opening.Kind));

    private Task Retire(Guid id) => TryAsync(() => Service.RetireAccountAsync(id));

    private Task Reopen(Guid id) => TryAsync(() => Service.ReopenAccountAsync(id));

    private Task Schedule() => TryAsync(() => Service.ScheduleAsync(
        Scheduling.AccountId!.Value,
        Scheduling.Description,
        Scheduling.Payee,
        JiranisokoTech.Domain.Common.Money.Of(
            (long)Math.Round(Scheduling.Amount * 100), "KES"),
        Scheduling.Every,
        Scheduling.StartsOn!.Value));

    private Task Pause(Guid id) => TryAsync(() => Service.PauseAsync(id));

    private Task Resume(Guid id) => TryAsync(() => Service.ResumeAsync(id));

    private Task Settle(Guid scheduleId, Guid chargeId) =>
        TryAsync(() => Service.SettleAsync(scheduleId, chargeId, Clock.Today));

    private Task Rename(Guid id) => TryAsync(() => Service.RenameAccountAsync(
        id, Request?.Request.Form["name"].ToString() ?? string.Empty));

    private async Task TryAsync(Func<Task> act)
    {
        Refusal = null;

        try
        {
            await act();
            Navigation.NavigateTo("/accounting", forceLoad: true);
        }
        catch (Exception exception) when (
            exception is InvalidOperationException or ArgumentException)
        {
            Refusal = exception.Message;
            await LoadAsync();
        }
    }

    private sealed class ScheduleInput
    {
        public Guid? AccountId { get; set; }

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "What the cost is.")]
        [StringLength(300)]
        public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Who it is paid to.")]
        [StringLength(200)]
        public string Payee { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        /*
         * Taken in whole units and converted to minor units on the way in, because that is
         * what somebody types. The conversion rounds rather than truncating: 1500.005 entered
         * by accident should be a cent out, not a cent short every month for a year.
         */
        [Range(0.01, 100_000_000)]
        public decimal Amount { get; set; }

        public Recurrence Every { get; set; } = Recurrence.Monthly;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "When it starts.")]
        public DateOnly? StartsOn { get; set; }
    }

    private sealed class OpenInput
    {
        [Required(ErrorMessage = "The code people will type.")]
        [StringLength(20)]
        public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "What the account is called.")]
        [StringLength(200)]
        public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        public AccountKind Kind { get; set; } = AccountKind.Expense;
    }
}
